  <section class="index__section" aria-label="Types of clothing manufacturing — OEM, ODM, private label and CMT">
    <div class="index__container">

      <header class="index__section-header">
        <span class="index__section-label">MANUFACTURING MODELS</span>
        <h2 class="index__section-title">Types of Clothing Manufacturing We Offer</h2>
        <p class="index__section-subtitle">Four B2B production models — OEM, ODM, Private Label, and CMT — each suited to a different stage of brand development. All handled in-house at our Dhaka and Narayanganj facilities. Compare models on our <a href="/clothing-manufacturers" class="index__link" title="Full clothing manufacturers guide">full manufacturing guide</a>.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="index__grid index__grid--2" style="margin-bottom:1px;">
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title">OEM — Original Equipment Manufacturing</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">You provide the design — whether a full tech pack, a reference sample, or a detailed brief — and we produce to your exact specification. Cutting, sewing, embellishment, quality inspection, and packaging all happen inside our <a href="/garments-factory" class="index__link" title="Garments factory Dhaka Bangladesh">apparel factory</a> in Dhaka. Your brand label is sewn in. The factory floor remains ours; the intellectual property and branding remain yours. This is the most common model for established fashion brands scaling production without building their own factory.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);font-size:0.8rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">Best for: Brands with confirmed designs ready for bulk production.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title">ODM — Original Design Manufacturing</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">We develop the base designs and you select from our seasonal collections, then customise fabric, colour, print, and trims to align with your brand identity. You receive a unique product with your own label — without the design development cost. ODM is popular with buyers who want speed to market without maintaining an in-house design team. Minimum 300 pieces per style applies.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);font-size:0.8rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">Best for: Brands that need market-ready designs with custom branding.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index__grid index__grid--2">
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title">Private Label Apparel Manufacturing</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">A complete factory-to-brand service where we handle everything from garment design and fabric sourcing to woven labels, hang tags, poly bag packaging, and final carton packing — all under your brand name. First-time brand founders get a finished product with professional retail presentation without coordinating multiple suppliers. Labels, packaging, and compliance documents included in the FOB price. See our <a href="/private-label-clothing-manufacturer" class="index__link" title="Private label clothing manufacturer Bangladesh">private label manufacturer</a> page for full details.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);font-size:0.8rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">Best for: Startup brands launching their first collection.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title">CMT — Cut, Make &amp; Trim</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">If you have already secured your fabric through your own supply chain — or you work with a specialist textile mill — our <a href="/cut-and-sew-service" class="index__link" title="CMT cut make trim garment service">CMT service</a> provides precision cut-and-sew production without the fabric supply component. You ship the fabric to our Narayanganj or Chittagong facility, our production team follows your tech pack, and finished garments are packed and shipped FOB. CMT rates are lower than full-package pricing because material risk stays with your supply chain.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);font-size:0.8rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);">Best for: Brands with established fabric suppliers who need a reliable sewing partner.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

