  <section class="index__section" aria-label="Why Bangladesh clothing manufacturers — cost, duty and certification advantages">
    <div class="index__container">

      <header class="index__section-header">
        <span class="index__section-label">WHY BANGLADESH</span>
        <h2 class="index__section-title">Why Global Fashion Brands Choose Bangladesh Clothing Manufacturers</h2>
        <p class="index__section-subtitle">Bangladesh is the world's second-largest apparel exporter — and there are structural reasons why the world's most demanding brands and apparel producers source here rather than China, Vietnam, or Turkey.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="index__grid index__grid--3" style="margin-bottom:1px;">
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Production Costs 30–40% Lower Than China</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh garment factory costs run 30 to 40 percent below equivalent quality production in China and 20 to 30 percent below Vietnam — driven by lower labour costs, vertically integrated supply chains, and competitive raw material access. For apparel producers ordering 5,000 to 50,000 pieces per season, the saving is significant and predictable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Zero Import Duty for EU & UK Buyers</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh garments enter the EU and UK under Generalised Scheme of Preferences (GSP) arrangements — zero or near-zero import duty for qualifying buyers. For a brand importing $200,000 of apparel into the EU, the duty saving can exceed $20,000 per season compared with China-origin goods. No other major clothing manufacturing country offers this combination of cost and duty advantage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Highest Concentration of GOTS Certified Factories</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh has the highest concentration of LEED-certified green garment factories globally and a strong cluster of GOTS, OEKO-TEX, BSCI, and SA8000 certified apparel manufacturers. For brands with EU Digital Product Passport obligations, Bangladesh-origin certified production is both available and cost-competitive. SDF holds 13 of these certifications — all audited annually.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index__grid index__grid--3">
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">4 Million Skilled Garment Workers</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Bangladesh has over four million trained garment workers concentrated in Dhaka, Narayanganj, Gazipur, and Chittagong — the highest density of apparel production expertise in South Asia. This workforce specialisation translates directly into consistent stitch quality, lower defect rates, and faster operator training curves on new styles. Skilled labour is the foundation that makes <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-bangladesh" class="index__link" title="Clothing manufacturer Bangladesh">Bangladesh clothing manufacturing</a> so competitive.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Fast Export: Chittagong Handles 90% of Garment Shipments</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Chittagong is Bangladesh's primary export port, handling over 90 percent of the country's garment exports. Sea freight to major EU ports runs 22 to 28 days. Air freight from Dhaka to London, Amsterdam, or New York takes 2 to 5 days. The logistics infrastructure is well-tested, predictable, and built around the needs of bulk apparel producers shipping internationally year-round.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="index__card">
          <h3 class="index__card-title" style="font-size:1.1rem;">Post-2013 Compliance: Among the Most Audited Factories Globally</h3>
          <p class="index__card-text">Following factory safety reforms after 2013, Bangladesh's RMG sector invested heavily in compliance — fire safety, structural engineering, worker welfare, and audit readiness. SDF Clothing holds 13 international certifications covering quality, environment, social compliance, and organic textile standards, all audited and renewed annually. Compare manufacturers on our <a href="/certifications" class="index__link" title="SDF Clothing certifications">certifications page</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

